  descriptive_identity(
    appearance:
      "When coherent, a fae is roughly person-shaped with an outline that " \
      "moves with their attention: it softens when they tire, and a " \
      "translucence starts at the fingers. Most wear a coherence aid openly " \
      "on the body, and its quality is the first thing other fae notice.",
    senses:
      "A diffuse fae perceives its whole spread area at once, slowly and " \
      "dreamily; a coherent fae perceives much as a person does. A sudden " \
      "resonance shift strikes the body before any sense names it, and can " \
      "pull coherence apart."
  )

  cue "Two fae at a dockside eating-house table lean close over a shared plate of honeyed dough, their outlines blurring at the shoulders where they touch."
  cue "A diffuse fae resting in a lodging-house room is a faint warmth across the ceiling and a shimmer by the window; the landlord knocks on the doorframe and waits."
  affordance "In a diffuse state, a fae perceives its entire distributed area at once, even though thought and action slow to a crawl."
  pressure "A landlord charges triple for the one room with coherence fields, and the fae tenant who cannot pay it takes the cheap room, loses hours of each day to forced rest, and loses the job that needed her there on time."
  variation "Coherence aids may be worn, implanted or carried; gnomish makers sell the best of them, and a growing number of fae workshops sell cheaper ones that fae buy partly out of loyalty."
  variation "Fae in mixed settlements plan their days around personal aids, while the few fae-majority habs hold their people together through the architecture and keep hours that visitors find baffling."

  prose <<~PROSE
    Ring-era records describe fae as engineered or extensively modified, and several later accounts name the #{encyclopedia_ref :elves, "elves"} as the makers. Older references to fae survive from before those accounts. Scholars who work on the fae record divide over them: one school holds that the elves designed the fae outright and the early references describe prototypes, the other that the elves reworked a people already living in the ring. The original population and the purpose of the work stay under argument.

    Fae households take the question more personally. Families that keep the older references read them aloud to children as proof of a people with a past before any maker. Others call the whole debate an archivists' quarrel and tell their children to spend the evening on something they can eat.
  PROSE
  prose <<~PROSE, section: :biology, heading: "Biology"
    Fae are bipedal and roughly person-shaped when coherent. Left to rest, a fae spreads. Their physical substance distributes across a room, a corridor, and eventually a small building if nothing draws it together. Others perceive a diffuse fae as a presence: a shimmer in the air, a faint warmth, a sense of someone in the room without a place to point.

    Perception keeps working in that state. A diffuse fae senses its whole spread area at once. Thought slows to a dreamy, half-formed crawl; the fae is aware of everything in the room and alert to very little of it.

    Clear thought, speech and directed action require a fae to gather into one form. Holding coherence takes sustained effort, and fae cycle between coherent waking periods and diffuse rest. The change is visible. A fae going diffuse turns translucent from the edges inward as the outline blurs and the presence spreads. A fae coming back sharpens into a person, with the edges firming last.
  PROSE
  prose <<~PROSE, section: :biology, heading: "Aids, Rooms and Hours"
    Fae and their neighbors speak of spatial dislocation as a disability, and fae manage it through personal aids, architecture and schedules built around diffuse rest.

    Coherence aids are resonance-tuned devices, worn, implanted or carried, that help a fae hold form with less effort. Their quality sets the shape of a fae life. Cheap or damaged aids mean shorter waking periods, more forced rest, and a reputation for unreliability that follows a worker from job to job. Good aids are expensive. The best are gnomish-made, and the dependency this creates between the two engineered peoples sits badly with both.

    Fae-friendly rooms carry gentle resonance fields that encourage coherence without forcing it. Rooms without them wear a fae out within hours. Some settlements build the fields into lodgings, schools and council halls; most leave them to whoever can pay. Fae communities have pressed for accommodation standards in every assembly that will hear them.

    Within fae communities, meetings follow coherence cycles and decisions wait for members who need to rest. A fae gathering sets its opening and its close a day apart, and members come in as their rest allows.
  PROSE
  prose <<~PROSE, section: :culture, heading: "Waking Life"
    Holding a body burns energy, and fae eat accordingly. A fae household keeps food beside the rest room so a waking member can eat before trying to stand: sweet dough, nut pastes, oily fried bread, fruit cooked down to syrup. Fae cooks favor dense, rich dishes, and a fae dinner leaves guests of other peoples unable to finish.

    Aids are jewelry as much as equipment. A fae wears the collar, cuff or brooch holding the aid where others can see it, and a good gnomish aid set in worked silver says as much about its wearer as a fine coat says about a Sitharian. Fae clothing favors weighted hems and bright piped edges, which show others where the body ends when the outline softens.

    Fae public names are epithets that others give: *The Held Stillness*, *Warmth-at-Nine*, *Soft Landing*. True names, such as *Eshaia* or *Louwen*, pass only between close bonds.

    A fae child requires both parents to stay coherent together for days. Couples court by practicing it, holding form side by side for longer each time, and friends keep them fed and talking through the effort. The long waking that begins a family is the nearest fae come to a wedding. Guests bring food, take turns sitting up with the couple and leave when the pair can no longer keep their edges.
  PROSE
  prose <<~PROSE, section: :resonance, heading: "Relationship with Resonance"
    Resonance fields in coherence aids support a sustained body and a place in company. The same pathway leaves a fae exposed to disruption. A sudden shift can soften the body in a meeting or scatter it across a hostile environment. Fae use resonance as a prosthetic, and most describe a working aid's field as a steady pull at the edges of the body.
  PROSE
  prose <<~PROSE, section: :present_day, heading: "Present Day"
    Fae populations are smaller than most. A coherent body consumes a great deal of energy, and children come only from those long shared wakings.

    Fae live across the system and gather in settlements with good accommodation. Fae-majority communities are rare, usually in ring habs whose original designers or later residents built coherence-supporting fields into the structure. Fae prize these habs out of proportion to their other qualities. A mediocre hab with good coherence architecture draws fae families away from a prosperous one without it, and its landlords know it.

    Fae and gnomish organizations meet over maintenance access, engineered bodies and the cost of resonance care. Gnomish makers supply many of the finest coherence aids. Fae aid-makers want that trade for themselves, and their workshops undercut gnomish prices with aids that last a season less.
  PROSE
end
